The `port_md/*` cluster is C mode-decision logic that is ported but not wired
into this pipeline -- their own module docs say so (lpd1_loop.rs: "PARTIAL ...
decisions only"). A 0 % row there means unwired, not untested, and the
distinction matters before anyone "fixes" the coverage.

WHAT THE COLD ROWS BOUGHT: A PANIC, NOW A REFUSAL
`port_picstruct_ra.rs` is the random-access picture structure and sat at 0.00 %
because all 40 encodes were FLAT (hierarchical_levels = 0). Probing the
uncovered path:

    SVTAV1_HIER_LEVELS=1  ->  rc=101, thread 'main' panicked at
    inter_md_arm.rs:747: "an inter candidate names reference N with no DPB
    picture -- ref_frame_type_arr and padded_by_ref disagree"

A hierarchical GOP makes picture decision name BWDREF/ALTREF references that
only the flat low-delay-P path fills. That is a caller-visible configuration
failing by PANIC, which docs/WORKING-ON-THIS.md §6 forbids outright. Now a
`gop_config_error` refusal (exit 3) naming the unwired wiring; the refusal
inventory goes 61 -> 62.

STILL UNPROBED, and each is a candidate for the same treatment: 10-bit video
(SVTAV1_BD=10 on the inter path), tiles on video, superres on video, and
intra_period 2/4 (both of which DO encode -- verified -- and were simply not in
the coverage grid).
